Subject: [PATCH] dxmt: a shared texture or buffer frees its allocation without its device (cranvr)

DXMT lets a device go before its resources, as the Direct3D 11 documentation allows. A shared texture or buffer
freed its D3DKMT allocation in its destructor through its device: `m_parent->GetLocalD3DKMT()`, a virtual call. An
application that released the device first crashed in that call. SteamVR's client in Steam does so when SteamVR quits
after a game: it releases shared textures after their device. Steam for Windows ended a few seconds after every SteamVR
run of Half-Life: Alyx (cranvr issue #197). Each of its six crash dumps shows
`~DeviceTexture` calling through a dead device: a call to address 0, to 0x9fa, or `__cxa_pure_virtual`.

- util_d3dkmt.h: `KmtDevice` holds a D3DKMT device and destroys it with its last reference.
- The DXGI device keeps its D3DKMT device in a `KmtDevice`. `GetKmtDevice` gives it out through IMTLDXGIDevice and
  MTLD3D11Device.
- A texture or buffer with an allocation keeps the `KmtDevice` and frees the allocation through it. The D3DKMT device
  thus lives until its DXGI device and its last shared resource let go.

---
diff --git i/src/d3d11/d3d11_buffer.cpp w/src/d3d11/d3d11_buffer.cpp
index b3422d2..4061ea7 100644
--- i/src/d3d11/d3d11_buffer.cpp
+++ w/src/d3d11/d3d11_buffer.cpp
@@ -29,6 +29,8 @@ private:
   /* cranvr: a buffer shared with D3D11_RESOURCE_MISC_SHARED (see d3d11_shared_buffer.hpp) */
   SharedBufferMemory shared_;
   D3DKMT_HANDLE local_kmt_ = 0;
+  // cranvr: the D3DKMT device of local_kmt_, which may outlive the buffer's device
+  Rc<KmtDevice> kmt_device_;
   D3DKMT_HANDLE global_kmt_ = 0;
 
   /* The shared path of the constructor: the buffer lies on the memory of a file mapping. `imported` is the memory
@@ -57,6 +59,8 @@ private:
       global_kmt_ = importedGlobal;
     } else if (!ShareBuffer(device, data, &local_kmt_, &global_kmt_)) {
       ERR("D3D11Buffer: no D3DKMT allocation for a shared buffer; it has no handle");
+    } else {
+      kmt_device_ = device->GetKmtDevice();
     }
     return true;
   }
@@ -144,12 +148,8 @@ public:
   }
 
   ~D3D11Buffer() {
-    if (local_kmt_) {
-      D3DKMT_DESTROYALLOCATION destroy = {};
-      destroy.hDevice = m_parent->GetLocalD3DKMT();
-      destroy.hResource = local_kmt_;
-      D3DKMTDestroyAllocation(&destroy);
-    }
+    if (local_kmt_ && kmt_device_)
+      kmt_device_->destroyAllocation(local_kmt_);
     if (shared_.mapping)
       CloseHandle(shared_.mapping);
   }
